{
  "participants": [
    {
      "login": "pablomartin4btc",
      "stance": "support",
      "note": "Approach ACK; argued that failing hard with CORRUPT is correct, contributed a unit test, and opened doc PR #35944 for wallet recovery guidance"
    },
    {
      "login": "polespinasa",
      "stance": "objection",
      "note": "Approach ACK initially, but objected that failing to load locks users without backups out of uncorrupted funds; also caught an invalid unit test"
    },
    {
      "login": "jonatack",
      "stance": "support",
      "note": "Concept ACK; suggested adding a release note"
    },
    {
      "login": "rkrux",
      "stance": "support",
      "note": "Concept ACK; supports failing fast on load rather than automatically attempting unreliable repairs"
    },
    {
      "login": "jeanpablojp",
      "stance": "objection",
      "note": "Approach ACK, but reported that stored and calculated hashes are inverted in the corruption error message"
    }
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "c:5367219157",
      "kind": "approach",
      "harm": "users with corrupted wallets who lack backups cannot access uncorrupted funds or export descriptors",
      "quote": "If we disable allowing this corrupted wallets, users that unconsciously did not create a backup will be unable to access any of their funds at all without switching to an old Core version.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "open",
      "author_replies": [
        "c:5375058547"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": false,
      "settled_by_id": "",
      "settled_by_quote": ""
    },
    {
      "id": "rc:3829019177",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "the unit test passes due to an EOF deserialization failure rather than exercising the hash mismatch corruption code path",
      "quote": "This test is wrong it is not testing the `DBErrors::CORRUPT` path intended to test.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "resolved",
      "author_replies": [
        "rc:3833484889"
      ],
      "fix_pushed": true,
      "settled_by_id": "rc:3833484889",
      "settled_by_quote": "Fixed"
    },
    {
      "id": "rc:3889367582",
      "kind": "correctness",
      "harm": "the error message inverts stored and actual hashes, causing users inspecting the database manually to look for the wrong key",
      "quote": "The two are swapped. In the description you call the DB key the stored hash and `wtx.GetHash()` the calculated one, and here the `strprintf` passes them the other way round.",
      "blocking": false,
      "status": "open",
      "author_replies": [],
      "fix_pushed": false,
      "settled_by_id": "",
      "settled_by_quote": ""
    }
  ],
  "support": [
    {
      "id": "r:4879267838",
      "verdict": "Approach ACK",
      "reason": "When a tx record's stored hash doesn't match the hash of its deserialized content, returning `NEED_RESCAN` was the wrong response: the rescan is not a reliable repair... failing hard with `CORRUPT` makes no unverifiable assumptions about what the DB was supposed to contain, and signals unambiguous failure rather than attempting an unreliable recovery.",
      "substantive": true
    },
    {
      "id": "r:4969917474",
      "verdict": "Approach ACK",
      "reason": "Aproach ACK\n\nHow can I test this?",
      "substantive": false
    },
    {
      "id": "c:5345686759",
      "verdict": "Concept ACK",
      "reason": "Concept ACK. Worth a release note?",
      "substantive": false
    },
    {
      "id": "c:5425655052",
      "verdict": "Concept ACK",
      "reason": "I do prefer the wallet to stop and fail fast instead of trying to fix rare corrupted scenarios automatically _everytime on load_, which makes the wallet do too much and bloats the codebase as well.",
      "substantive": true
    },
    {
      "id": "r:5060820855",
      "verdict": "Approach ACK",
      "reason": "Built it, ran the unit tests and the wallet functional tests, and reproduced the corruption on regtest.",
      "substantive": true
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Dropped the previous assessment's claim on recovery guidance from pablomartin4btc as it was a documentation suggestion handled via separate PR #35944 rather than an objection to merging this PR. Added jeanpablojp's open report of inverted hash parameters in the error message string, and kept polespinasa's open approach concern regarding fund lockout for users without backups."
}
